# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Toyota Yaris XP210 five-door hatchback, 2020 onwards.
#
# The fourth-generation Yaris, sold in Britain as a hybrid only. UK on sale
# 3 August 2020, first customer deliveries September 2020, at £19,910 Icon,
# £20,970 Design, £21,920 Dynamic, £22,220 Excel and £24,005 Launch Edition,
# on the road. Replaced the XP130 after nine years.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/all-new-toyota-yaris-hybrid-launched-with-special-retail-offers/
# https://xr793.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/2021-Toyota-Yaris-UK.pdf
#
# Dimensions 3.940 x 1.745 x 1.495 m, wheelbase 2.560 m, the European figures.
# Source: English Wikipedia, "Toyota Yaris (XP210)" infobox: European wheelbase
# 2,560 mm, length 3,940 mm, European width 1,745 mm, European height
# 1,470-1,500 mm. The hull measures 1.745 m wide with the roof at 1.495 m and
# the wheel centres 2.560 m apart; the assembly is 3.959 m long with the plates
# and 1.940 m wide over the mirrors.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-side view from a motor show, not a strict
# elevation, so the flank was built from it and from images 2 to 4 with the
# wheel centres fixed by the published ratio. The blue car in image 4 carries a
# contrasting black roof; the model does not, because the paint material covers
# the roof and the two-tone option is a trim variant rather than a body shape.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB names from the 2021 brochure, evidence grade (a):
# Pure White, Platinum White Pearl, Tyrol Silver, Decuma Grey, Eclipse Black,
# Tokyo Red, Titan Bronze and Galactic Blue. Four are modelled: Tyrol Silver,
# Pure White, Decuma Grey and Tokyo Red. Weights silver 3, white 3, grey 2,
# red 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h, the hybrid's quoted maximum. Comfort 105/488, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 105: a modern, quiet supermini, a step above the XP130. Classes
# 0,1,2: it is the cheapest hybrid small car in the range and drifts down the
# wealth bands as it ages, and the modern Very-low band needs a car that is not
# a luxury model.
#
# Dates are road presence: August 2020 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026)
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp210.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp210.dae (54 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-yaris-xp210/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear side glass ends too sharply and the rear
# quarter lacks the photograph's flare; the headlamp and bumper contours are
# angular; the rear window is too small and too steeply raked; the bonnet
# creases are shallow; the contrasting roof is deliberately not modelled. The
# top view and the raised turn confirm a continuous body-coloured roof. At
# 128 px the upright hatch, the squared-off tail and the large lower grille
# read as the XP210.

obj=citycar
name=ToyotaYarisXP210(TyrolSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2020
intro_month=8
#retire_year=2035
#retire_month=6
speed=175
length=3
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=105
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=488

